# Terrain Representation Redesign — Shipped

The prior GPU investigation was measurement-only; this goal required an **engine architecture change**. That is now implemented and verified.

## What changed

Greedy quad generation is **unchanged** (`ChunkData`, `_build_mesh*`, incremental dirty-column patches). The **render representation** is new:

| Before (legacy) | After (default) |
|-----------------|-----------------|
| 1 `MultiMesh` box instance per terrain quad | 1 `ArrayMesh` per chunk (`terrain_surface_mesh`) |
| `cull_disabled` + fragment `discard` on 5/6 faces | `cull_back` face-only geometry |
| Worker builds `terrain_buffer` | Worker skips terrain buffer; main thread bakes mesh from quads |
| `representation=multimesh_legacy` | `representation=surface_mesh` |

Ramps stay on MultiMesh (wedge/corner/prism).

### New / modified files

- `helpers/chunk_surface_mesh_builder.gd` — face-only mesh from greedy quads
- `shaders/ChunkSurfaceMesh.gdshader` + `.tres` — atlas UVs, face shading
- `chunks/chunk_view.gd` — emits surface mesh + ramp MultiMesh
- `chunks/chunk_mesh_buffer_builder.gd` — representation flag, skips terrain buffer when surface
- `chunks/chunk_manager.gd` — `terrain_surface_mesh` config wiring
- `config/performance_quality_config.gd` — `terrain_surface_mesh=true` on all presets
- `scripts/verify_terrain_surface_representation.gd` — A/B harness

