## Executive Conclusion

**The renderer is not the steady-state bottleneck at medium preset with RENDER_DISTANCE=2.**

GPU submission stays modest (~61–71 draw calls, ~9k–14k primitives/frame). Frame time regressions during streaming come from **main-thread work outside steady-state GPU geometry** — chunk mesh build, crystal simulation, and deferred MultiMesh buffer uploads — not from rising draw counts.

