### Not directly exposed (proxies documented)

| Area | Status | Proxy used |
|------|--------|------------|
| **Render-thread ms** | Godot 4 Forward+ does not expose per-frame render-thread time to GDScript | Frame max spikes (253 ms) with flat draw counts |
| **CPU/GPU sync** | No explicit fence API | Spike pattern + upload queue depth |
| **Pipeline compilations** | Counter always 0 in probe | No shader recompile during session |

**Note on `chunk_upload_ms` in F3:** `PerfProfiler` sections use cumulative `last_us` (lifetime total), not per-frame. F3 shows 25.49 ms (idle) / 51.96 ms (stream end) as **total time spent in `chunk_upload` scope since boot**, not per-frame cost. Per-frame upload work is scoped in `ChunkManager._drain_deferred_mesh_buffers` via `profiler.begin/end("chunk_upload")` with a 3500 µs budget, draining 1 buffer/frame (`ChunkView.drain_pending_buffer_uploads`).

**Note on `untracked_ms`:** Because section `last_us` is cumulative but `_frame_us` is per-frame, `untracked_ms` clamps to 0 once cumulative tracked time exceeds one frame — so it is **not a reliable render-wait proxy** in the current profiler design. Do not use it for bottleneck calls.

