```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A[Main loop ~25-34ms avg] --> B{Measured GPU submission}
    B --> C[~61-71 draw calls]
    B --> D[~9k-14k primitives/frame]
    B --> E[7-8 texture bindings]
    A --> F[Non-render main-thread work]
    F --> G[Crystal sim - cumulative 1892ms idle / 2807ms stream]
    F --> H[Chunk mesh build - cumulative 4958ms idle / 10277ms stream]
    F --> I[Chunk upload drain - 1 buffer/frame, 3.5ms budget]
    A --> J[Frame spikes to 253ms]
    J --> K[NOT correlated with draw call increase]
    J --> L[Correlated with mesh build + streaming + upload queue depth max 5]
```

### Terrain rendering path (what the GPU receives)

1. Each loaded chunk view owns multiple `MultiMeshInstance3D` nodes (greedy-merged quads as scaled box instances).
2. One shared `ShaderMaterial` + atlas for boxes; one shared ramp material.
3. Instance custom data carries atlas tile + face code; fragment shader discards wrong faces.
4. Buffer uploads are **deferred**: `enqueue_buffer_upload` → queue → `drain_pending_buffer_uploads(1, budget_us)` on main thread.

**Evidence:** `chunks/chunk_view.gd` (enqueue/drain), `chunks/chunk_manager.gd` (upload budget + profiler scope), shader above.

