## Crystal renderer redesign complete

Crystal **simulation is unchanged** — only the visual path was replaced. Production now renders procedural quartz-like cluster geometry via instanced `MultiMeshInstance3D` layers.

### Architecture

| Layer | Role |
|-------|------|
| `helpers/crystal_cluster_mesh.gd` | Procedural pyramid clusters, LOD tiers (6/12/18 tris), neighbor-mask rotation |
| `crystal/crystal_chunk_layer.gd` | Instanced rendering; env toggle `legacy` \| `procedural` (default: procedural) |
| `crystal/crystal_manager.gd` | Per-chunk LOD from player distance; neighbor masks at rebuild time only |
| `crystal/crystal_cell.gd` | Render-only `neighbor_mask` (not saved) |

**LOD (per chunk, 1 draw call/chunk):**
- Distance ≥ 2 → 1 pyramid (6 tris)
- Distance 1 → 2 pyramids (12 tris)
- Distance 0 → 3 pyramids (18 tris)

**Growth sockets / branches:** Cardinal neighbor depth mask rotates each cluster toward adjacent crystal cells (visual only).

**Animation hook:** `neighbor_mask` + depth are available at rebuild/patch time for future shader or custom-data animation.

